3. Sequence: `s1 = malloc(n1 + 1)`. If `n1` is negative-converted to ~0xFFFFFFFF, `n1+1` wraps to 0 (32-bit arithmetic before promotion to `size_t`), so `malloc(0)` may succeed; later `s1[n1] = '\0'` writes far out of bounds (OOB write / heap overflow).
